     "text": "North: Summer (Direct rays)\nSouth: Winter (Indirect rays)",
     "size": 26,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "December: Northern Winter",
   "say": "Six months later, in December, Earth is on the opposite side. The Northern Hemisphere tilts away, while the Southern Hemisphere enjoys summer.",
